1
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:11,919
What are you doing?

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,679
Bringing your memory back.

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:14,839
Stop it.

4
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:17,039
- What are you two doing?
- Cha.

5
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,279
We're up here to look at
the architectural drawings.

6
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,240
<i>Open it then. I'd love to see them too.</i>

7
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:24,760
<i>If she's the real Claire,</i>

8
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,599
<i>she'll have a scar on her back.</i>

9
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:28,879
<i>You're still up, Grandpa.</i>

10
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,840
<i>Let me talk to Chan for a bit.</i>

11
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:35,080
<i>I hope you haven't forgotten
the promise you made to me.</i>

12
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,479
What are you hiding in there?

13
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:42,840
Let me see.

14
00:00:43,520 --> 00:00:45,199
There's nothing about you in here.

15
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,160
If that's true,
why won't you let me see it?

16
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:50,719
- Let me see.
- I said it's nothing.

17
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,319
Are you hiding something else?

18
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:54,079
You must be hiding something from me.

19
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:56,999
- What are you doing? It's nothing.
- I don't care. Let me see.

20
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,400
- Hey.
- Hey.

21
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:18,440
Well...

22
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:23,640
I, NITCHAN SATHITPHONG, PROMISE THAT
I WILL ONLY MARRY KHAEDARUN KANCHATHARA.

23
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,480
This is...

24
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:28,040
You wanted to know so badly, right?

25
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,320
I'm sorry.

26
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,680
Let me ask you something.

27
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:00,240
What did you promise her grandfather?

28
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:13,280
I promised him I would protect
and take care of Claire with my life.

29
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:22,880
In that case, I'll get out of your hair.

30
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,840
I'm sorry.

31
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:48,440
I'm sorry I snapped at you.

32
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:51,760
I guess I was missing Claire.

33
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,119
Um, I...

34
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,800
I'm sorry too.

35
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:00,720
I didn't know you were missing her.

36
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:06,360
Chan? Chan.

37
00:03:07,960 --> 00:03:09,999
Uh, sorry.

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,639
I can come back.

39
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,720
Oh, I'm just leaving.

40
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:28,480
Hope I'm not interrupting.

41
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:37,120
If Ms. Claire were still alive,

42
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:40,400
you would've married her by now.

43
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,280
<i>I'm sorry I snapped at you.</i>

44
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:19,560
<i>I guess I was missing Claire.</i>

45
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:29,320
Hey.

46
00:05:30,520 --> 00:05:31,840
What are you doing here?

47
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,440
I...

48
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:36,960
I was just lost in my thoughts.

49
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,280
What about you?

50
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,240
I followed you out here.

51
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,400
I want you to wear this bracelet.

52
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,520
Fine.

53
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,319
I'm telling you,

54
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:21,119
I'm accepting this bracelet

55
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:23,719
not because I'm softening up.

56
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:27,319
I just thought that if I were Ms. Claire,
she would've accepted it.

57
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,440
She wouldn't have cared.

58
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:49,160
Are you done?

59
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,040
Then I'm off.

60
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:22,200
Why is being Ms. Claire so exhausting?

61
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,720
Yes?

62
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:49,520
It's me.

63
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:51,920
What is it?

64
00:07:58,400 --> 00:07:59,560
I...

65
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:03,040
I missed you.

66
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,320
Claire.

67
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:47,840
No.

68
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,680
I'm not Ms. Claire.

69
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,080
I know.

70
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,640
Well, then...

71
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:07,400
Tonight...

72
00:09:08,640 --> 00:09:10,240
can you be her for me?

73
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,360
What do you mean?

74
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,120
<i>Ms. Claire?</i>

75
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:27,360
<i>Excuse me?</i>

76
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:31,840
Ms. Claire, excuse me?

77
00:09:38,040 --> 00:09:39,080
Ms. Claire?

78
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:40,800
Yes?

79
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:45,440
There are people here
to see you at the pool.

80
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:49,080
Okay, I'll be right down.

81
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,600
Ms. Patch, Ms. Yo.

82
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:21,080
See? I told you
Ms. Claire wasn't mad at us.

83
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,080
What's going on?

84
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,639
The leak, of course.

85
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,479
Well...

86
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:32,320
We were worried,
so we wanted to clear things up with you.

87
00:10:32,960 --> 00:10:36,239
With the leak, we thought you did it.

88
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,439
And you probably thought we did it.

89
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:42,439
But actually, there might be someone else
who wants to ruin all of us.

90
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,559
Exactly.

91
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:46,680
So we came up with the best way out.

92
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:48,800
How?

93
00:10:52,440 --> 00:10:54,839
By becoming actual friends.

94
00:10:54,840 --> 00:10:58,679
This way, people can't criticize you
for hiring us to be your friends.

95
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,680
How does that sound?

96
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:04,520
Well...

97
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:06,880
Okay.

98
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,720
Then we should celebrate our friendship.

99
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,079
Tonight?

100
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,599
Yes, tonight.

101
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,560
Oh, let's make it some other day.

102
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,239
Why, Ms. Claire?

103
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,719
Or are you still mad at us?

104
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:25,559
No, it's just that it's getting late.

105
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,959
Oh, Ms. Claire.

106
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,879
How is this late?

107
00:11:29,880 --> 00:11:31,399
The night's still young.

108
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:35,599
It's going to be a long night. Please.

109
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:37,079
- Please come.
- Please.

110
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:38,119
- Please.
- Please.

111
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,999
- Come with us, Ms. Claire.
- Please, come.

112
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,720
Please, please, please.

113
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:51,200
Here, Ms. Claire,
right this way. Take it in.

114
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,520
Guys, look who's here!

115
00:11:58,240 --> 00:12:00,039
- Ms. Claire!
- Hello!

116
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:02,639
- She's gorgeous.
- She's beautiful.

117
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:03,760
Look at her.

118
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,359
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

119
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:10,120
Whoo!

120
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:15,399
- Ms. Claire...
- Wow, are you the real Ms. Claire?

121
00:12:15,400 --> 00:12:17,120
Uh, yes.

122
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:23,279
Let me tell you, we've been
wanting to meet you for a long time.

123
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,239
Right, guys?

124
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:26,280
- Yes!
- Yeah!

125
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,919
Alright, why don't you sit here?

126
00:12:29,920 --> 00:12:32,440
- Come on.
- What about you two?

127
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,279
Don't worry.

128
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:37,679
Yo and I need to take care of something.
We'll be right back.

129
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,679
Okay? Got, take care of her.

130
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,159
- You got it.
- Sit right here.

131
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:43,040
- Sit right here.
- Wait here.

132
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,840
- Take care of her, Got.
- You got it.

133
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,879
Uh, I'll go get you a drink, Ms. Claire.

134
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:52,999
No, thank you.

135
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,920
Just a little. I'll be back.

136
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:59,199
Ms. Claire, can I take a photo with you?

137
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:00,200
Sure.

138
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:09,199
You saw us, right?

139
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:11,680
I brought Ms. Claire like you wanted.

140
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:22,079
I did exactly what you wanted.

141
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,480
Give me Ms. Claire's contract.

142
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:28,880
Sure.

143
00:13:31,760 --> 00:13:32,600
What's this?

144
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,439
You're so annoying.

145
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,200
Don't pretend you don't know these drugs.

146
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:47,320
You're already familiar
with them, aren't you?

147
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:54,359
Put this drug in Claire's drink.

148
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:57,199
Once she passes out, take her to a room.

149
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:00,439
After the job's done,
I'll give you the contract

150
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,919
and delete this video.

151
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:04,479
- What the hell are you doing?
- What's wrong?

152
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:07,120
You think I won't leak it? Try me.

153
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:13,840
Cha.

154
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:16,119
I think you've done enough.

155
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,759
What are you up to now?

156
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,439
You can see that's Claire.

157
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:21,159
But I don't believe it.

158
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,640
The real Claire has a scar on her back.

159
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:25,719
And what if she doesn't?

160
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:27,040
Then she's fake.

161
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,360
And what if she has the scar?

162
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:34,279
That's even better.

163
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:37,160
Because I've prepared
a lot of fun things for her.

164
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:42,320
Whether she's real or fake,
she won't survive tonight.

165
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,680
What are you up to now?

166
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:47,959
Chris, picture this.

167
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:50,799
Her passing out for just one night,

168
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:54,800
then waking up and finding out
she has three lovers all at once.

169
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:58,400
It's gonna be so much fun.

170
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,279
Here you go, Ms. Claire.

171
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:13,799
Oh, no, thank you. I'd rather not.

172
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:17,560
Come on, this is a party.
Have a drink to enjoy yourself.

173
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:22,399
Uh, in that case,
I'll just have plain water.

174
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,919
Come on now, Ms. Claire.

175
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:29,319
We're partying.
You can't have plain water.

176
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,519
Have this instead.

177
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:33,919
Orange juice,
perfect for an angel like you.

178
00:15:33,920 --> 00:15:35,120
Okay, then.

179
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:38,439
Oh, wait.

180
00:15:38,440 --> 00:15:39,679
Guys!

181
00:15:39,680 --> 00:15:42,759
Today, Ms. Claire
agreed to be our friends.

182
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:46,120
So let's raise a glass to her!

183
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:52,959
Cheers!

184
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,640
Bottoms up.

185
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,639
Oh, just a little bit more.

186
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:08,959
- Oh.
- Please?

187
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:09,880
Okay.

188
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:17,080
Let's have fun.

189
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,360
Just a bit.

190
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,799
You should have told me
that you were coming,

191
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,400
so I could accommodate you better.

192
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:53,560
Get me at my office when you're done.

193
00:16:56,640 --> 00:17:00,000
I think we should move
Ms. Claire's body to our hospital.

194
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:02,240
I don't trust this place.

195
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,079
Keep her here.

196
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,920
No one here knows Claire.

197
00:17:07,760 --> 00:17:10,639
If anyone thinks of looking for her body,

198
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:13,480
no one would expect us to keep her here.

199
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:37,560
Uh, I think it's starting to get late.

200
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,839
I should head back.

201
00:17:39,840 --> 00:17:41,199
Oh, no.

202
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,959
You can't, Ms. Claire.
You haven't even been here an hour.

203
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:45,119
Stay a bit longer.

204
00:17:45,120 --> 00:17:46,880
Please, Ms. Claire.

205
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,800
Oh, please stay, Ms. Claire.

206
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:51,959
Oops. Ms. Claire?

207
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,240
What's wrong?

208
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:56,080
Sit, sit. You should sit down.

209
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,079
Why do I feel so dizzy?

210
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,560
Please sit down.

211
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:03,840
Are you okay?

212
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,279
Ms. Patch, what did you give me?

213
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:20,080
Orange juice.

214
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,759
You must be getting a contact high.

215
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:24,040
Don't worry.

216
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:26,959
I'll have my friend take you to rest.

217
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:27,999
- Got!
- Got!

218
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,480
Take Ms. Claire to rest.

219
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,640
Let me take you, Ms. Claire.

220
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:33,840
Let's go, Ms. Claire.

221
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:35,879
Uh, I'm fine.

222
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:38,039
You're very drunk. You should rest.

223
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,400
- I'm fine. I'll figure it out...
- Let's go.

224
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,039
Get off me. Get off.

225
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,360
Get off me!

226
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:47,159
- Ms. Claire, stay with us, please.
- Let go.

227
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:48,080
Ow!

228
00:19:13,920 --> 00:19:15,119
Ms. Claire?

229
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:17,119
Where are you, Ms. Claire?

230
00:19:17,120 --> 00:19:19,159
We won't hurt you.

231
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:20,079
Come out.

232
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:21,960
Please come out.

233
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,559
Don't just stand there.

234
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:28,039
The door won't
open itself. Go find the key.

235
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,600
Go find the key.

236
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,679
I got the key.

237
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,280
Open it. Open it now.

238
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,479
Got it?

239
00:19:56,480 --> 00:19:57,840
- Got it?
- Got it.

240
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,559
Search.

241
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:08,480
Ms. Claire?

242
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,040
- Where are you?
- Ms. Claire.

243
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,520
Where are you?

244
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,160
- Where the hell is she?
- Where are you?

245
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,480
Where is Claire?

246
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:31,720
She came into this room,
but she was gone once we got in.

247
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,439
The window.

248
00:20:34,440 --> 00:20:36,760
It's open. She must've got out this way.

249
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,280
Claire?

250
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,200
Carry her to the bed.

251
00:21:18,960 --> 00:21:19,960
Get out.

252
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,679
Hey.

253
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,160
What are you gonna do to me?

254
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:33,000
Nothing much.
I just want to check something.

255
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:35,079
But don't worry.

256
00:21:35,080 --> 00:21:38,280
Because you won't remember anything
when you wake up.

257
00:22:21,680 --> 00:22:23,400
Is it done?

258
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:27,000
Tell them to handle her,
film her and send me the video.

259
00:22:27,600 --> 00:22:28,719
Cha.

260
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:30,080
Don't do this, Cha.

261
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:31,600
Why not?

262
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,360
Or you want to do it yourself?

263
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:48,800
Let's go, guys.

264
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:00,160
Man.

265
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:04,520
Wow.

266
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:10,119
I've always wondered how sweet
socialites taste.

267
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:13,079
So sweet, dudes. Here we go.

268
00:23:13,080 --> 00:23:13,999
Let's see.

269
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,599
We should get some evidence, right?

270
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:18,919
Yeah, let's do it.

271
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,880
- Right?
- Do it, dude.

272
00:23:23,640 --> 00:23:24,679
Who's next?

273
00:23:24,680 --> 00:23:25,799
Film it for me too.

274
00:23:25,800 --> 00:23:28,320
Yeah, you go next. I'll finish it off.

275
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:33,559
Is this a good idea, Patch?
You know who Ms. Claire is.

276
00:23:33,560 --> 00:23:37,399
What are we supposed to do?
If we refuse, Ms. Cha will ruin us.

277
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:40,479
Let them do it
and send the video to Ms. Cha.

278
00:23:40,480 --> 00:23:41,720
We'll delete it later.

279
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,080
Let me have a sniff.

280
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:10,520
- Where is Ms. Claire?
- Whoa.

281
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:25,000
I asked where she is.

282
00:24:47,360 --> 00:24:48,600
What is it, Mom?

283
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,319
I came to ask you about Claire.

284
00:24:51,320 --> 00:24:54,200
Have you figured out
if she's the real Claire?

285
00:24:56,200 --> 00:25:01,000
But looking at you,
I think I've got my answer.

286
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:05,959
Think carefully
before you do anything next time.

287
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:07,320
Don't get carried away.

288
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:09,080
So what next?

289
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:12,639
Don't worry about that, Mom.

290
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:16,079
Your job is to do whatever it takes
to make Dad love and trust you again.

291
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:19,160
As for Claire, I'll handle her.

292
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:21,520
How?

293
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:25,239
Are you gonna tell your Dad
she isn't the real Claire

294
00:25:25,240 --> 00:25:28,240
just because that stupid scanner
didn't recognize her face?

295
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,640
Do you think he'll believe you?

296
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:37,119
We can't prove it right now
whether she's real or an impostor,

297
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:39,000
but we can at least show Dad that

298
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:43,559
letting his no-good, troublemaker
grandchild return to run the company

299
00:25:43,560 --> 00:25:46,000
will only bring disgrace to our business.

300
00:25:48,560 --> 00:25:51,439
Last night, I watched a moral drama.

301
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:53,359
Claire was the protagonist.

302
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:56,000
It's called...

303
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:59,280
"The Wicked Grandchild
and Her Seven Lovers."

304
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:01,480
Wanna watch it?

305
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:14,239
SEND ME THE VIDEO WHEN IT'S DONE.

306
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:15,160
What?

307
00:26:15,840 --> 00:26:17,000
Why isn't it here?

308
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:18,680
What isn't here?

309
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:23,640
PATCHY

310
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,520
Hey.

311
00:26:30,040 --> 00:26:33,719
I told you last night to send me the video
after you handled Claire.

312
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:35,600
So did you handle her or not?

313
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:42,039
Cha! Hey!

314
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:43,400
What happened last night?

315
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:45,759
Can you not right now?

316
00:26:45,760 --> 00:26:47,999
I told you I'd tell you later.

317
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,359
Hey.

318
00:26:49,360 --> 00:26:50,919
Where are you going now?

319
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:54,960
You must be in a hurry to get rid of
the evidence from last night.

320
00:26:56,640 --> 00:26:58,039
What evidence?

321
00:26:58,040 --> 00:27:01,240
The evidence of you hiring people
to gang rape Claire.

322
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,879
What the hell are you doing?

323
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,919
Give it here. What are you trying to do?

324
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:12,879
What are you doing?

325
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:15,760
- Chan.
- What are you trying to do?

326
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:19,359
What are you trying to do?

327
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:20,800
Were you filming?

328
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:23,160
Get the hell out.

329
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:25,000
Get out!

330
00:27:28,760 --> 00:27:31,319
Claire? Claire?

331
00:27:31,320 --> 00:27:34,840
Claire? Can you hear me, Claire?

332
00:27:35,920 --> 00:27:36,800
Claire?

333
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:44,039
What did you give her?

334
00:27:44,040 --> 00:27:45,159
I don't know.

335
00:27:45,160 --> 00:27:47,079
Ms. Cha gave it to me.

336
00:27:47,080 --> 00:27:49,040
But I think it's a date rape drug.

337
00:27:49,840 --> 00:27:51,159
It was Ms. Cha's order.

338
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:52,800
We had nothing to do with it.

339
00:27:53,400 --> 00:27:55,040
Check the phone.
Delete all the videos of her.

340
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:56,639
You got it.

341
00:27:56,640 --> 00:27:57,960
DELETE

342
00:27:59,840 --> 00:28:00,680
Claire?

343
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:03,720
Claire? Claire?

344
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:06,280
Claire, can you hear me? Claire?

345
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:07,720
Claire?

346
00:28:09,120 --> 00:28:11,360
Claire? Claire?

347
00:28:12,760 --> 00:28:15,840
You've targeted Claire many times before.

348
00:28:16,520 --> 00:28:18,399
But this time you've gone too far.

349
00:28:18,400 --> 00:28:21,400
How do you know
it was me? Do you have proof?

350
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:25,640
My proof is the witness
who called me to rescue Claire.

351
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:29,680
Aren't you curious

352
00:28:30,480 --> 00:28:32,479
how I knew where Claire was,

353
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:34,480
and how I saved her in time?

354
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:41,000
This is the last time I'll let it slide.

355
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:43,480
If something like this happens again,

356
00:28:45,280 --> 00:28:48,160
I'll use the power the chairman
gave me to take decisive action.

357
00:28:56,480 --> 00:28:57,360
Cha.

358
00:28:58,200 --> 00:29:01,000
Tell me everything
that happened last night.

359
00:29:01,640 --> 00:29:03,200
How did Chan find out?

360
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:07,999
Cha! Cha, come back here, Cha!

361
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:09,280
Cha!

362
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:12,520
Chris!

363
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:18,120
- Where's your phone?
- Why, Cha?

364
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:20,560
- What's wrong?
- Give me your phone.

365
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:31,120
Cha.

366
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:35,200
Cha. Hey, Cha.

367
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:37,480
Cha, why are you looking through my phone?

368
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:40,080
Cha.

369
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,319
Cha.

370
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:45,080
RECENT OUTGOING CALLS

371
00:29:46,600 --> 00:29:48,440
Will you tell me what's going on?

372
00:29:50,440 --> 00:29:52,280
How did Chan save Claire last night?

373
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:56,600
- What?
- How did Chan know where Claire was?

374
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:03,320
Wait. Did you think I called him?

375
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,759
Why would I do that, Cha?

376
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:08,919
Because you're a dog in the manger.

377
00:30:08,920 --> 00:30:10,840
You didn't wanna share her.

378
00:30:11,720 --> 00:30:12,639
Cha.

379
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:15,599
You know I was with you all night.

380
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:17,720
When could I call Chan?

381
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:24,880
Maybe Chan had that bodyguard follow us.

382
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:31,760
Go get dressed.

383
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,960
Where are we going?

384
00:30:39,920 --> 00:30:42,200
Well, if you want me to trust you,

385
00:30:43,040 --> 00:30:44,800
you gotta prove yourself to me.

386
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:19,479
I never expected you to call me.

387
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:20,839
<i>Mr. Chan, listen to me.</i>

388
00:31:20,840 --> 00:31:24,479
You need to save Ms. Claire.
I don't have time to explain.

389
00:31:24,480 --> 00:31:29,200
Ms. Cha's having people gang rape her
and film a video to blackmail her.

390
00:31:32,080 --> 00:31:34,080
I'll send you the location. I have to go.

391
00:31:40,800 --> 00:31:43,600
<i>You called to find out
if Ms. Claire's safe, right?</i>

392
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:45,959
I know about that now.

393
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:47,119
Cha came to see me.

394
00:31:47,120 --> 00:31:49,479
And she wanted to know who told you.

395
00:31:49,480 --> 00:31:51,360
You don't have to worry.

396
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:53,360
I didn't tell her anything.

397
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,480
Where am I?

398
00:33:06,680 --> 00:33:08,240
Why am I wearing this?

399
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:17,840
Hey.

400
00:33:21,680 --> 00:33:22,560
You're awake.

401
00:33:23,200 --> 00:33:25,600
Are you hungry? I made you breakfast.

402
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:30,960
How did I end up here?

403
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:33,840
Well, you passed out.

404
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:37,280
I brought you here
so the chairman wouldn't suspect anything.

405
00:33:40,320 --> 00:33:42,120
Uh, and...

406
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:45,160
who changed my clothes?

407
00:33:49,040 --> 00:33:49,880
Don't tell me...

408
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,000
You...

409
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,520
How could you do that to me?

410
00:33:59,320 --> 00:34:00,680
Didn't want me to see?

411
00:34:02,160 --> 00:34:03,320
Actually,

412
00:34:04,480 --> 00:34:05,839
I've seen more than this.

413
00:34:05,840 --> 00:34:07,239
Hey!

414
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:11,639
Have you forgotten that
the body standing in front of me

415
00:34:12,320 --> 00:34:13,719
is the body I gave you?

416
00:34:15,440 --> 00:34:17,359
If you're holding that over my head,

417
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:21,199
ask yourself if I even wanted
this body you gave me.

418
00:34:21,800 --> 00:34:24,079
You claim you saved my life,

419
00:34:24,080 --> 00:34:26,239
but you have no right
to violate my body like this.

420
00:34:27,040 --> 00:34:28,320
Let's just say...

421
00:34:28,920 --> 00:34:31,159
I didn't do anything inappropriate.

422
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,440
So,

423
00:34:34,880 --> 00:34:36,159
what do you remember?

424
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:42,879
I...

425
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:47,039
remember Ms. Yo and Ms. Patch
taking me to someone's house.

426
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:48,600
Cheers!

427
00:34:51,679 --> 00:34:53,520
And suddenly I felt drowsy

428
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:56,279
and groggy, and...

429
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,639
Uh, I'm fine.

430
00:34:57,640 --> 00:34:58,799
You're very drunk.

431
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:00,159
- Let's go, Ms. Claire.
- Let go of me.

432
00:35:00,160 --> 00:35:01,520
Get off me!

433
00:35:05,160 --> 00:35:07,640
I remember men trying to assault me.

434
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:12,800
Ms. Cha tricked you into going there.

435
00:35:15,080 --> 00:35:16,320
Ms. Cha tricked me?

436
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:19,240
Why would she do that?

437
00:35:20,520 --> 00:35:24,040
She wanted to prove
if you are the real Claire.

438
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:25,920
How?

439
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:29,160
How would she know if I'm the real Claire?

440
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,800
Well...

441
00:35:32,840 --> 00:35:35,120
The real Claire had a scar on her back.

442
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:38,840
What?

443
00:35:39,360 --> 00:35:42,679
Now what are we going to do?

444
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:44,880
So Ms. Cha knows I'm not the real Claire.

445
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:52,239
If someone like Ms. Cha found out
you weren't the real Claire,

446
00:35:52,240 --> 00:35:54,080
would she let you stay here?

447
00:35:55,440 --> 00:35:56,520
What do you mean?

448
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:59,160
I don't have a scar on my back.

449
00:36:56,840 --> 00:36:58,880
Why do I have a scar like Ms. Claire?

450
00:37:01,880 --> 00:37:03,320
Didn't I tell you before?

451
00:37:04,680 --> 00:37:07,039
I didn't make you look like Claire.

452
00:37:07,040 --> 00:37:09,160
I made you be her.

453
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:11,439
And it's not just the scar.

454
00:37:11,440 --> 00:37:14,039
You must be identical to her.

455
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:16,079
I would give you
a blood transfusion if I could.

456
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:18,079
But I'm not Ms. Claire.

457
00:37:18,080 --> 00:37:19,559
My name is Jinla.

458
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:21,079
Hold on, hey.

459
00:37:21,080 --> 00:37:22,599
- Hey. Hey...
- Let go. Let go.

460
00:37:22,600 --> 00:37:24,719
- Listen to me.
- I said let go! Let go!

461
00:37:24,720 --> 00:37:26,759
Hey, let me go! Let go!

462
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:28,320
I said let go!

463
00:37:49,360 --> 00:37:50,440
What is this?

464
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,960
I asked what this is.

465
00:37:55,560 --> 00:37:57,800
Why is it inside the bracelet you gave me?

466
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:07,120
Why is there a GPS?

467
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:14,600
You used me as bait.

468
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:18,880
You knew Ms. Cha was going
to do something like this to me.

469
00:38:23,920 --> 00:38:26,000
Since the incident at the vault,

470
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:30,200
I knew Ms. Cha wondered
whether you were the real Claire.

471
00:38:30,840 --> 00:38:33,520
And someone like her
would find a way to prove it.

472
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:41,480
What's going on?

473
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:45,199
Look, do whatever it takes
to get him here ASAP.

474
00:38:45,200 --> 00:38:47,240
Tell him I'll pay extra.

475
00:38:52,520 --> 00:38:56,279
The biometric scanner at the vault
detected that she isn't Ms. Claire.

476
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:57,800
And Ms. Cha knows about it?

477
00:38:59,320 --> 00:39:01,439
Ms. Claire's doctor just called me.

478
00:39:01,440 --> 00:39:04,840
Said Ms. Cha asked about
the scar on Ms. Claire's back.

479
00:39:06,840 --> 00:39:08,040
A scar on her back?

480
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:14,159
<i>So I figured Ms. Cha
would find a way to look at your back.</i>

481
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:15,720
<i>Until...</i>

482
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:20,639
<i>I saw Yo and Patchy show up.</i>

483
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:24,519
See? I told you
Ms. Claire wasn't mad at us.

484
00:39:24,520 --> 00:39:25,919
What's going on?

485
00:39:25,920 --> 00:39:28,919
Then we should celebrate our friendship.

486
00:39:28,920 --> 00:39:30,359
- Please, Ms. Claire.
- Let's go.

487
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:31,559
- Please.
- Let's go.

488
00:39:31,560 --> 00:39:34,039
- Please come with us.
- Let's go.

489
00:39:34,040 --> 00:39:35,919
Please, please, please.

490
00:39:35,920 --> 00:39:37,440
- Let's go, come on.
- Please.

491
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:40,279
- Yay, she says yes!
- Let's go.

492
00:39:40,280 --> 00:39:42,640
- Let's go.
- Come on.

493
00:39:47,120 --> 00:39:49,120
How is it? Is the signal okay?

494
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:51,040
It's working properly.

495
00:39:52,040 --> 00:39:54,559
But are you sure you want to do this?

496
00:39:54,560 --> 00:39:56,560
Ms. Cha could hurt Ms. Jin.

497
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:02,040
We need Ms. Cha to see that scar
with her own eyes.

498
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:05,640
<i>So I had to let them drug you</i>

499
00:40:07,160 --> 00:40:09,560
<i>so she'd believe you are the real Claire.</i>

500
00:40:10,520 --> 00:40:13,480
<i>Because the only one who can
make Ms. Cha stop doubting you</i>

501
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,520
<i>is Ms. Cha herself.</i>

502
00:40:16,280 --> 00:40:17,719
What the hell are you doing?

503
00:40:17,720 --> 00:40:18,999
What are you trying to do?

504
00:40:19,000 --> 00:40:21,320
What are you trying to do, huh?

505
00:40:22,240 --> 00:40:23,079
Were you filming?

506
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:25,280
Claire? Claire?

507
00:40:26,040 --> 00:40:27,240
<i>But the plan went wrong because...</i>

508
00:40:28,040 --> 00:40:28,679
Claire?

509
00:40:28,680 --> 00:40:31,120
<i>I'd thought Ms. Cha would stop there.</i>

510
00:40:36,400 --> 00:40:37,760
I trusted you.

511
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:41,600
I've done everything you said.

512
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:47,240
But you turned me into a tool.

513
00:40:49,400 --> 00:40:51,239
What else was I supposed to do?

514
00:40:51,240 --> 00:40:52,999
Did you have another way?

515
00:40:53,000 --> 00:40:57,080
You know when Ms. Cha suspects something,
she will stop at nothing.

516
00:40:58,720 --> 00:41:00,920
I have a way to make everything stop.

517
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:07,760
I will tell everyone I'm not Ms. Claire.

518
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:10,160
My name is Jinla.

519
00:41:10,920 --> 00:41:13,480
The woman
whose life you've turned into hell.

520
00:41:14,880 --> 00:41:15,960
Just like that,

521
00:41:17,480 --> 00:41:18,760
everything stops.

522
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:24,080
And do you think I'd let you do that?

523
00:41:24,880 --> 00:41:25,880
Why not?

524
00:41:26,440 --> 00:41:27,560
What are you gonna do?

525
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:30,120
Are you gonna kill me?

526
00:41:32,200 --> 00:41:34,560
Or are you gonna make me disappear?

527
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:37,000
Go ahead.

528
00:41:39,480 --> 00:41:40,440
Do it.

529
00:41:41,880 --> 00:41:43,440
I know you won't dare.

530
00:41:44,520 --> 00:41:46,719
Because if you do anything to me,

531
00:41:46,720 --> 00:41:48,600
Ms. Claire will disappear too.

532
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:57,640
No, she won't.

533
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:04,920
I'll just find another woman
to replace you as Claire.

534
00:42:08,640 --> 00:42:09,880
You're well aware.

535
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:15,200
The Kanchathara family
has enough money to buy anyone's life.

536
00:42:17,400 --> 00:42:19,360
I'll just have to find...

537
00:42:20,600 --> 00:42:24,400
another woman to replace you as Claire.

538
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:31,240
But let's not complicate things.

539
00:42:32,920 --> 00:42:34,600
You're just angry right now.

540
00:42:36,800 --> 00:42:39,040
Go home and calm down.

541
00:42:39,720 --> 00:42:41,600
I'll handle the rest myself.

542
00:43:07,680 --> 00:43:10,640
Oh, hey. Are you okay?

543
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:29,239
<i>I'll just find another woman</i>

544
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:31,240
<i>to replace you as Claire.</i>

545
00:44:00,120 --> 00:44:01,880
I hate you!

546
00:44:03,080 --> 00:44:06,240
I hate you. I hate you.

547
00:44:25,880 --> 00:44:26,840
What happened?

548
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:29,280
Why did she look so angry?

549
00:44:30,800 --> 00:44:34,280
It's nothing.
I just reminded her of her place.

550
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:36,400
So she knows.

551
00:44:40,520 --> 00:44:41,760
What did you want?

552
00:44:43,840 --> 00:44:44,800
Chan.

553
00:44:46,240 --> 00:44:47,960
I think Ms. Claire was murdered.

554
00:44:51,960 --> 00:44:53,240
What do you mean?

555
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:56,440
The police called
about the pilot's blood test.

556
00:44:57,080 --> 00:44:59,120
They found GHB in his blood.

557
00:45:10,000 --> 00:45:11,040
Sir?

558
00:45:13,880 --> 00:45:15,400
Here is what you requested.

559
00:45:22,160 --> 00:45:23,480
Thank you, Captain.

560
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:41,240
That pilot was really drugged.

561
00:46:08,480 --> 00:46:10,160
I hate you.

562
00:46:13,120 --> 00:46:16,920
I hate you! Do you hear me? I hate you!

563
00:46:21,200 --> 00:46:22,280
<i>Chan.</i>

564
00:46:23,600 --> 00:46:25,559
<i>The day you dropped off Ms. Claire,</i>

565
00:46:25,560 --> 00:46:27,240
was there anything unusual?

566
00:46:28,040 --> 00:46:29,080
Unusual?

567
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:30,639
Like what?

568
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:34,159
Like the pilot's demeanor or behavior.

569
00:46:34,160 --> 00:46:37,439
Did he look dazed, or unwell, or anything?

570
00:46:37,440 --> 00:46:40,999
Because GHB takes about
20 minutes to take effect.

571
00:46:41,000 --> 00:46:45,720
So I need to know if the pilot showed
any symptoms before taking off.

572
00:46:50,200 --> 00:46:51,319
Good morning, Captain.

573
00:46:51,320 --> 00:46:52,599
Good morning.

574
00:46:52,600 --> 00:46:53,999
It's a beautiful day.

575
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:55,759
Visibility should be great.

576
00:46:55,760 --> 00:46:57,479
The sky is clear today.

577
00:46:57,480 --> 00:47:01,560
I've been instructed to fly around
the project site with no landing, correct?

578
00:47:02,160 --> 00:47:06,439
Yes. Let's wait and see
if Ms. Claire wants anything extra.

579
00:47:06,440 --> 00:47:08,679
Alright. If you'll excuse me.

580
00:47:08,680 --> 00:47:10,800
- Sure. Thank you.
- Sure.

581
00:47:15,120 --> 00:47:15,959
I don't think so.

582
00:47:15,960 --> 00:47:18,680
He looked perfectly normal to me.

583
00:47:19,520 --> 00:47:22,760
Then how did GHB
end up in the pilot's blood?

584
00:47:35,840 --> 00:47:38,999
Given the time for
the drug to take effect,

585
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:42,159
the pilot must have been drugged
before he boarded.

586
00:47:42,160 --> 00:47:44,720
And the only one
who can tell us what happened is...

587
00:47:51,640 --> 00:47:52,720
Ms. Jinla.

588
00:48:23,840 --> 00:48:24,959
<i>Why is the chairman at the office?</i>

589
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:28,039
<i>Is this about
Ms. Cha's suspicion about Ms. Jin?</i>

590
00:48:28,040 --> 00:48:30,159
The facial scanner outside the vault

591
00:48:30,160 --> 00:48:33,079
suddenly didn't
recognize Claire's face, Dad.

592
00:48:33,080 --> 00:48:34,639
You just won't stop, will you?

593
00:48:34,640 --> 00:48:37,399
If you don't want
my dad to switch the project,

594
00:48:37,400 --> 00:48:39,200
<i>just bring Claire here now.</i>

595
00:48:39,880 --> 00:48:41,240
Can we open the door now?
